  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This maple is one of the late Henry Hohman's selections. Hohman's ability to select outstanding plants for propagation was one of his well-known attributes. 'The Bishop' has seven-lobed, fairly deeply divided purple-red leaves balancing between the Palmatum and Matsumurae Groups. The leaves measure 6-7 cm long and 7-8 cm wide, with slender petioles 4-5 cm long. The lobes extend outward and are divided about three-quarters of the way to the leaf base. Each lobe is oblong-ovate, gradually tapering to a long slender point. The margins are uniformly and finely serrated. The purple red is bright in the spring and does not bronze until late summer. The fall color is an excellent crimson. This upright-growing tree is vigorous and hardy, and reaches 4 m at maturity."
  },
